From b750dc658082cd4d89d4397b9c575980cf5ef6dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Lane A <lane-a@local.invalid>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:54:57 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 15/18] feat(live): audio excitement, reaction scan on the
 buffer, fuser and quick preview

Live MVP step 2 (LIVE_CLIPPING off; not wired to routes/workers yet).

- live/signals.py: per-half-second loudness + >1 kHz loudness of each new
  buffer segment; CAUSAL robust z (each point against the baseline before
  it, cached), so later level changes never rewrite history.
- live/reaction_scan.py: runs the existing Phase 2 streamer reaction picker
  (mic channel, scream/laugh, facecam, game events, named trigger) on the
  last N s of the buffer and returns its moments on the wall clock; drops
  "silent_action" (event, no reaction), as build_reaction_hints does.
  Plain loudness found nothing on the Kai stream sample (max z 1.6); the
  picker finds the vocal burst at 02:01 ("full-screen colour flash followed
  by a large on-screen banner").
- live/fuser.py: candidates from reaction moments, audio-confirmed chat
  spikes, and strong sustained audio; chat alone never clips; rejected
  spikes (spam/bots/raids) ignored; chat right after a reaction boosts it;
  configurable pre/post-roll, cap, de-duplication, optional visual veto;
  weak picker items (< 0.3) dropped.
- live/preview.py: 9:16 720p ultrafast preview from a buffer window.
- live/buffer.py: concat list uses absolute paths (relative session dirs
  broke the cut).
- tools/live/demo_fake_live.py: plays a recorded stream as live through the
  real recorder; scans, fuses, cuts and previews while it plays; logs
  per-stage latency.

Measured (fake-live, Kai sample, CPU): previews render 5-16 s after a
candidate is confirmed; detection latency is 2-5 min, dominated by the
reaction scan (~100 s per 120 s window). Not yet meeting the 30-40 s
target: next step is a fast voice-only first pass with the face analysis
only on promising windows.
Tests: test_live_fuser 10/10, test_live_buffer 6/6.

